text:
lex (design): Quick heads up 1: I prototyped a dark-mode heatmap and some focus-ring tweaks. Want feedback before I finalize tokens for the console.

tara (frontend): Share swatches? Especially interested in how the heatmap behaves at 1px and on retina vs non-retina.

lex (design): Pasted CSS vars + a small SVG pattern for legend hatching. Heatmap gradient runs deep teal -> indigo -> lime. Swatches: --heat-0: #04232b, --heat-1: #0b5f57, --heat-2: #0f92a3, --heat-3: #6a6cff, --heat-4: #bfe46a. Legend hatch uses a 45deg diagonal pattern for the top bucket.

owen (product): Lime for high values feels optimistic but might read as success instead of severity. Can we invert meaning or add explicit icon?

lex (design): Good call. I mapped lime to "high activity" and added an amber overlay for "alerts" bucket only. Also added legend labels: Active / Idle / Degraded / Alert.

sam (frontend): For focus rings, current white outline on dark surfaces is harsh. Proposal: use a 2px ring with --focus: rgba(167, 218, 255, 0.18) plus a 1px inner stroke of --focus-accent: #8bbfff so keyboard nav is visible but not blinding.

tara (frontend): That should avoid CLS jumps if we do it with box-shadow rather than outline. Need to check with high-contrast mode too.

lex (design): Also changed code block background to a near-terminal shade: #02161a and bumped monospace weight to 500 for readability. Added inline code bg: #031b1f with subtle border.

owen (product): Small copy nit: change legend header from "Activity" to "Request density" in heatmap and add unit tooltip: "requests / minute".

lex (design): Done. Also reduced chart grid opacity from 12% to 8% so the grid recedes on dark theme. Sample CSS snippet coming.

lex (design): CSS vars and pattern (inline):
```css
:root[data-theme=\"dark\"] {
  --bg: #071217;
  --surface-1: #0d1618;
  --text-main: #d7e9f2;
  --mono-weight: 500;
  --code-bg: #02161a;
  --code-inline-bg: #031b1f;
  --focus: rgba(167,218,255,0.18);
  --focus-accent: #8bbfff;
  --heat-0: #04232b;
  --heat-1: #0b5f57;
  --heat-2: #0f92a3;
  --heat-3: #6a6cff;
  --heat-4: #bfe46a;
  --alert-overlay: rgba(255,160,78,0.16);
}
```

lex (design): SVG hatch (small): `<pattern id=\"diagHatch\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" width=6 height=6 patternTransform=\"rotate(45)\"><line x1=0 y=0 x2=0 y2=6 stroke=\"rgba(0,0,0,0.12)\" stroke-width=1/></pattern>`

sam (frontend): Will try to plug these in. Two immediate checks: (1) contrast for --text-main on surface cards, and (2) heat-2 vs heat-3 at small cell sizes, especially for users with deuteranopia.

tara (frontend): For (2) we can add pattern overlay only when user enables high-contrast or when color difference < threshold. That keeps default clean.

aria-bot: Accessibility check queued. Tests: contrast ratios, color-blind palette diff, focus-visible rules. Report ETA ~8m. :robot_face:

dev-bot: Visual diff job started for branch: design/dark-heatmap-2024. CI job id: 89234.

aria-bot: Accessibility report: flagged items -> 1) --text-main contrast on .chip (needs >=4.5:1), 2) heat-2 vs heat-3 contrast low for deuteranopia, 3) focus ring visible but not announced to screen readers; add aria-focused states.

lex (design): Thanks. Action items: A) tweak --text-main to #cdeaf7 for chips, B) switch heat-3 from #6a6cff -> #6a86ff (cooler) and add optional crosshatch for heat-3 when color-diff low, C) add `role=\"img\" aria-label` on SVG legends and ensure `:focus-visible` maps to same box-shadow.

sam (frontend): I'll add the aria attributes and the optional pattern toggle (`prefers-contrast: more` + user setting). Will also test on low-end GPUs for shader-heavy charts.

nowen (product): Please update the release note blurb: "Dark theme: refreshed heatmap palette, improved focus rings, terminal-style code blocks, and accessibility patterns for color-difference users." Short and customer-facing.

lex (design): Will draft. If aria-bot clears second run I'll open the PR with assets and a small demo page.

dev-bot: Visual diff complete. 3 changed screenshots, 1 approved, 2 require review (heatmap legend and chart grid).

aria-bot: Re-run report: all items resolved except heatmap pair on 1x cell size for deuteranopia. Recommendation: enable legend hatch by default at <=8px cell size.

lex (design): Fine with that fallback. I'll enable the hatch for small cells and push the update. PR incoming.

sam (frontend): Ping me once PR is open, I'll review the visual diffs and accessibility changes.

nowen (product): Thanks all 1 :thumbsup: This iteration looks much better for customers using dark consoles.
